#!/bin/bash
# omarock-doctor: what's set up for omarock and what isn't, with a hint for each
# problem. It only reads: it changes nothing, plays nothing, and never prints a
# key, token or password (only whether the file is there, and its mode).
#
#   tools/omarock-doctor
set -uo pipefail
ok() { printf '  \e[32m✓\e[0m %s\n' "$*"; }
bad() { printf '  \e[31m✗\e[0m %s\n' "$*"; }
note() { printf '  \e[33m–\e[0m %s\n' "$*"; }
head2() { printf '\n\e[1m%s\e[0m\n' "$*"; }
active() { systemctl --user is-active --quiet "$1"; }
private_file() {  # FILE WHAT [WHERE IT COMES FROM]: present and mode 600?
  if [[ ! -e $1 ]]; then bad "$2: $1 is missing${3:+ ($3)}"; return 1; fi
  local mode; mode=$(stat -c %a "$1")
  if [[ $mode != 600 ]]; then bad "$2: $1 is mode $mode (chmod 600 it)"; return 1; fi
  ok "$2: $1 (mode 600)"
}
# DIR...: those there in which something is open to other accounts.
open_to_others() {
  local d
  for d; do [[ -d $d && -n $(find "$d" -perm /077 ! -type l -print -quit 2>/dev/null) ]] && printf '%s\n' "${d/#"$HOME"/\~}"; done
}
conf_value() { grep -E "^[[:space:]]*$2[[:space:]]" "$1" 2>/dev/null | head -1 | sed -E 's/^[[:space:]]*[a-z_]+[[:space:]]+"?([^"]*)"?.*/\1/'; }
# X-Omarock: omarock's own services answer only requests that carry it. A
# reply goes to python3 on stdin, never on its command line (others on this
# machine can read that): omarock-sxm's can name the account.
health() { curl -s -m 5 -H 'X-Omarock: 1' "$1/v1/health" 2>/dev/null; }

id=marcewing.omarock
plugin=$HOME/.config/omarchy/plugins/$id
shelljson=$HOME/.config/omarchy/shell.json
setting() {  # KEY DEFAULT: omarock's setting: its own file's, else (before 0.6) its entry in shell.json
  python3 -I - "$HOME/.config/omarock/settings.json" "$shelljson" "$id" "$1" "$2" <<'EOF'
import json, sys
mine, path, plugin, key, default = sys.argv[1:]
try:
    v = json.load(open(mine)).get(key)
    if v is not None:
        print(str(v).lower() if isinstance(v, bool) else v)
        sys.exit(0)
except Exception:
    pass
try:
    d = json.load(open(path))
    for items in (d.get("bar", {}).get("layout", {}) or {}).values():
        for it in items:
            if isinstance(it, dict) and it.get("id") == plugin and key in it:
                v = it[key]
                print(str(v).lower() if isinstance(v, bool) else v)
                sys.exit(0)
except Exception:
    pass
print(default)
EOF
}

head2 "Omarchy"
if command -v omarchy >/dev/null; then ok "Omarchy $(omarchy version 2>/dev/null)"; else bad "omarchy isn't installed: omarock is a plugin for Omarchy's bar"; fi

head2 "mpd"
if command -v mpd >/dev/null; then
  v=$(mpd --version 2>/dev/null | head -1 | grep -oE '[0-9]+\.[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?' | head -1)
  if [[ $(printf '%s\n0.24\n' "$v" | sort -V | head -1) == 0.24 ]]; then ok "mpd $v"; else bad "mpd $v: omarock needs 0.24 or later"; fi
else
  bad "mpd isn't installed"
fi
if active mpd || active mpd.socket; then ok "mpd is running"; else bad "mpd isn't running: systemctl --user enable --now mpd (or mpd.socket)"; fi
if [[ $(systemctl --user show mpd -p Restart --value 2>/dev/null) == no ]]; then
  note "mpd stays down if it crashes: ./install offers a drop-in that brings it back (mpd.service.d/restart.conf)"
fi
sock=$(setting socket "")
[[ -z $sock ]] && sock=${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/run/user/$(id -u)}/mpd/socket
if [[ -S $sock ]]; then
  if command -v mpc >/dev/null && MPD_HOST=$sock mpc status >/dev/null 2>&1; then ok "mpd answers on $sock"
  else note "$sock exists (install mpc to check that mpd answers on it)"; fi
else
  bad "no mpd socket at $sock: README.md, Install, 1. mpd"
fi
conf=${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/mpd/mpd.conf
for f in "$conf" "$HOME/.mpdconf" "$HOME/.mpd/mpd.conf"; do [[ -f $f ]] && { conf=$f; break; }; done
# mpd has no logins: on TCP, every account here can read its queue (with
# Apple Music, the private address of the Mac's stream) and change it.
tcp=$(ss -ltnpH 2>/dev/null | awk '/"mpd"/ {print $4}' | sort -u | paste -sd' ' -)
if active mpd.socket; then
  note "mpd.socket opens TCP port 6600 on every network interface, where every account here, and your network, can reach mpd: systemctl --user disable --now mpd.socket, then ./install"
elif [[ -n $tcp ]]; then
  if grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*bind_to_address[[:space:]]+"?[^"/~@[:space:]]' "$conf" 2>/dev/null \
     || ! grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*bind_to_address' "$conf" 2>/dev/null; then
    fix="./install offers to turn that off"
  else
    fix="mpd.conf has no TCP address now: systemctl --user restart mpd"
  fi
  note "mpd also listens on TCP ($tcp), where every account here can read its queue (with Apple Music, the stream's private address): $fix"
else
  ok "mpd listens on its socket only"
  if systemctl --user show-environment 2>/dev/null | grep -q '^MPD_HOST='; then ok "MPD_HOST points mpd clients at it"
  else note "mpc and other mpd clients need MPD_HOST=$sock to find mpd (./install offers it)"; fi
  if ! systemctl --user show mpd-mpris -p ExecStart --value 2>/dev/null | grep -q -- '-network unix'; then
    bad "mpd-mpris looks for mpd on TCP, so the media keys don't reach it: ./install gives it the socket"
  fi
fi
# mpd's files: a playlist saved from the queue while Apple Music plays holds
# the private address of the Mac's stream.
mask=$(systemctl --user show mpd -p UMask --value 2>/dev/null)
pid=$(systemctl --user show mpd -p MainPID --value 2>/dev/null)
running=""
[[ ${pid:-0} != 0 ]] && running=$(awk '/^Umask:/ {print $2}' "/proc/$pid/status" 2>/dev/null)
mdirs=("$(dirname "$conf")")
for key in playlist_directory db_file state_file sticker_file; do
  p=$(conf_value "$conf" "$key")
  [[ -n $p ]] || continue
  p=${p/#\~/$HOME}
  [[ $key == playlist_directory ]] || p=$(dirname "$p")
  [[ $p == "$HOME"/* ]] && mdirs+=("$p")
done
music=$(conf_value "$conf" music_directory)
music=${music/#\~/$HOME}
for i in "${!mdirs[@]}"; do
  [[ -n $music && (${mdirs[$i]} == "$music" || $music == "${mdirs[$i]}"/*) ]] && unset 'mdirs[i]'
done
mapfile -t mdirs < <(printf '%s\n' "${mdirs[@]}" | sort -u | awk 'kept == "" || index($0, kept "/") != 1 {print; kept = $0}')
mapfile -t open < <(open_to_others "${mdirs[@]}")
if [[ -n $mask ]] && (((8#$mask & 8#077) != 8#077)); then
  note "mpd writes its playlists, database and state for every account here to read (a playlist saved from the queue while Apple Music plays holds the stream's private address): ./install offers a drop-in (mpd.service.d/private.conf)"
elif [[ -n $running && $running != "$mask" ]]; then
  note "mpd still writes its files for every account, from before its drop-in: systemctl --user restart mpd"
fi
if ((${#open[@]})); then
  note "mpd's files are readable by every account here, in ${open[*]}: ./install makes them yours alone"
elif [[ -n $mask ]] && (((8#$mask & 8#077) == 8#077)); then
  ok "mpd's files are yours alone"
fi
if active mpd-mpris; then ok "mpd-mpris is running (media keys)"; else note "mpd-mpris isn't running: the media keys won't reach mpd (systemctl --user enable --now mpd-mpris)"; fi

head2 "The plugin"
if [[ -f $plugin/manifest.json ]]; then
  ok "omarock $(python3 -I -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))["version"])' "$plugin/manifest.json") in $plugin"
else
  bad "omarock isn't installed: omarchy plugin add https://github.com/marcewing/omarock --enable"
fi
if grep -q "\"$id\"" "$shelljson" 2>/dev/null; then ok "on the bar"; else note "not on the bar: omarchy plugin enable $id"; fi
loaded=$(journalctl --user -b --no-pager 2>/dev/null | grep -o "omarock [0-9.]* loaded" | tail -1)
[[ -n $loaded ]] && ok "the shell says: $loaded" || note "the shell hasn't logged omarock loading this boot"
printf '  sources: radio %s, spotify %s, appleMusic %s, siriusXM %s\n' \
  "$(setting radio true)" "$(setting spotify false)" "$(setting appleMusic false)" "$(setting siriusXM false)"
mapfile -t open < <(open_to_others "$HOME/.config/omarock" "$HOME/.local/share/omarock" "$HOME/.local/state/omarock" \
  "$HOME/.cache/omarock" "$HOME/.local/lib/omarock-mpris" "$HOME/.local/lib/omarock-soloist" \
  "$HOME/.local/share/omarock-soloist" "$HOME/.cache/omarock-soloist")
if ((${#open[@]})); then note "omarock's files are readable by every account here, in ${open[*]}: omarock makes them yours alone as it loads (or ./install)"
else ok "omarock's files are yours alone"; fi

head2 "omarock's sound output (the audio bus; optional)"
if [[ -f $HOME/.local/share/omarock/audio/omarock-bus.conf ]]; then
  pin=$(grep -o 'target.object = "[^"]*"' "$HOME/.local/share/omarock/audio/omarock-bus.conf" | cut -d'"' -f2)
  ok "installed, pinned to $pin"
  if pactl list sinks short 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $2}' | grep -qx -- "$pin"; then ok "that output is connected"; else note "that output isn't connected now: the bus waits, silent"; fi
  if active omarock-bus; then ok "omarock-bus is running"; else bad "omarock-bus isn't running: systemctl --user start omarock-bus"; fi
  if active omarock-guard; then ok "omarock-guard is running"; else note "omarock-guard isn't running: systemctl --user start omarock-guard"; fi
  if command -v mpc >/dev/null && MPD_HOST=$sock mpc outputs 2>/dev/null | grep -q "(omarock)"; then ok "mpd plays into the bus"
  else note "mpd's output isn't the bus: audio/README.md, step 3"; fi
else
  note "not set up (./install sound, or Set up… in omarock's settings): audio/README.md"
fi

if [[ $(setting spotify false) == true ]] || [[ -e $HOME/.config/systemd/user/omarock-spotify.service ]]; then
  head2 "Spotify"
  # Soloist itself, read without running it: the build you downloaded, and
  # whether it was checked with omarock's shim (its unit starts no other).
  so=$("$(dirname "$0")/update-soloist" status --installed 2>/dev/null | jq -c '.installed // empty')
  if [[ -z $so ]]; then
    bad "Soloist isn't installed: download it from Spotify, then ./install spotify (spotify/README.md, step 4)"
  else
    days=$(jq -r .days <<<"$so")
    if [[ $(jq -r .checked <<<"$so") != true ]]; then
      bad "this Soloist hasn't been checked with omarock (it's new, or was replaced by hand), so its unit won't start it again: ./install spotify, or Update… in omarock's settings (Spotify)"
    elif ((days >= 90)); then
      bad "Soloist's build is $days days old and has stopped working: download a new one from Spotify, then ./install spotify"
    elif ((days >= 80)); then
      note "Soloist's build is $days days old, and stops working at 90: download a new one from Spotify, then ./install spotify"
    else
      ok "Soloist$(jq -r '.version // empty | " " + .' <<<"$so"), built $days days ago, checked with omarock"
    fi
  fi
  [[ -f $HOME/.config/omarock/spotify.json ]] && ok "the developer app: ~/.config/omarock/spotify.json" || bad "no ~/.config/omarock/spotify.json: spotify/README.md, step 2"
  private_file "$HOME/.config/omarock/soloist-key" "the Soloist key" "spotify/README.md, step 3"
  if [[ $(setting spotify false) != true ]]; then
    note "switched off in omarock's settings: its services are stopped"
  else
    for u in omarock-soloist omarock-spotify; do active $u && ok "$u is running" || bad "$u isn't running: journalctl --user -u $u"; done
  fi
  # Soloist's command line, which every account here can read, should hold
  # "@key" in place of its key, and its control port should be guarded:
  # both by omarock-soloist-shim.so, which says so in its log. Read, never shown.
  if active omarock-soloist; then
    pid=$(systemctl --user show -p MainPID --value omarock-soloist)
    if tr '\0' '\n' <"/proc/$pid/cmdline" 2>/dev/null | grep -qx -- '@key'; then ok "Soloist's key isn't on its command line"
    else bad "Soloist's key is on its command line, where every account here can read it: Update… in omarock's settings (Spotify), or tools/install-spotify --start"; fi
    run=$(systemctl --user show -p InvocationID --value omarock-soloist)
    if journalctl --user --no-pager -q -o cat "_SYSTEMD_INVOCATION_ID=$run" 2>/dev/null | grep -q '^omarock-soloist: guards 127\.0\.0\.1:'; then
      ok "only your account reaches Soloist's control port"
    else
      bad "Soloist's control port isn't guarded (no word from omarock's shim): Update… in omarock's settings (Spotify), or tools/install-spotify --start"
    fi
  fi
  h=$(health "$(setting spotifyService http://127.0.0.1:8730)")
  if [[ -n $h ]]; then
    python3 -I -c '
import json, sys, time
h = json.load(sys.stdin); s = h.get("soloist", {}); w = h.get("web", {})
print("  " + ("\033[32m✓\033[0m" if s.get("loggedIn") else "\033[31m✗\033[0m") + " Soloist " + ("is signed in" if s.get("loggedIn") else "isn'"'"'t paired yet: spotify/README.md, step 5"))
print("  " + ("\033[32m✓\033[0m" if w.get("signedIn") else "\033[31m✗\033[0m") + " the Web API " + ("is signed in" + (", until " + time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d", time.localtime(w["signInEndsAt"])) if w.get("signInEndsAt") else "") if w.get("signedIn") else "isn'"'"'t signed in: tools/omarock-sp login"))
' <<<"$h"
  else
    bad "omarock-spotify doesn't answer"
  fi
fi

if [[ $(setting siriusXM false) == true ]] || [[ -e $HOME/.config/systemd/user/omarock-sxm.service ]]; then
  head2 "SiriusXM"
  private_file "$HOME/.config/omarock/siriusxm.json" "the account" "tools/install-sxm makes it: sxm/README.md"
  if [[ $(setting siriusXM false) != true ]]; then
    note "switched off in omarock's settings: omarock-sxm is stopped"
  else
    active omarock-sxm && ok "omarock-sxm is running" || bad "omarock-sxm isn't running: journalctl --user -u omarock-sxm"
  fi
  h=$(health "$(setting sxmService http://127.0.0.1:8720)")
  if [[ -n $h ]]; then
    python3 -I -c '
import json, sys
h = json.load(sys.stdin)
good = h.get("account") and h.get("loggedIn")
print("  " + ("\033[32m✓\033[0m signed in" if good else "\033[31m✗\033[0m not signed in" + (": " + h["error"] if h.get("error") else ": check ~/.config/omarock/siriusxm.json")))
' <<<"$h"
  else
    bad "omarock-sxm doesn't answer"
  fi
fi

if [[ $(setting appleMusic false) == true ]] || [[ -e $HOME/.config/omarock/apple.json ]]; then
  head2 "Apple Music"
  h=""
  bridge=$(setting appleBridge "")
  if [[ -z $bridge && -f $HOME/.config/omarock/apple.json ]]; then
    bridge=$(python3 -I -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(open(sys.argv[1])).get("bridge",""))' "$HOME/.config/omarock/apple.json" 2>/dev/null)
  fi
  [[ -n $bridge ]] && ok "the bridge: $bridge" || bad "no bridge address: ~/.config/omarock/apple.json (apple-bridge/README.md)"
  tokenfile=$(setting appleTokenFile "$HOME/.config/omarock/bridge-token")
  tokenfile=${tokenfile/#\~/$HOME}
  private_file "$tokenfile" "the bridge's token" "apple-bridge/README.md, the Linux side"
  if [[ -n $bridge ]]; then
    h=$(health "$bridge")
    if [[ -n $h ]]; then
      python3 -I -c '
import json, sys
h = json.load(sys.stdin)
print("  " + ("\033[32m✓\033[0m the bridge answers, and may use Apple Music" if h.get("authorized") else "\033[31m✗\033[0m the bridge answers, but Apple Music access isn'"'"'t allowed on the Mac yet"))
' <<<"$h"
      # Bridge 0.9.0 announces itself over Bonjour, if the Mac lets it.
      if [[ $(python3 -I -c 'import json, sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin).get("bonjour", ""))' <<<"$h" 2>/dev/null) == denied ]]; then
        note "the bridge doesn't announce itself on the network (the Mac's Local Network access for omarock bridge is off), so setup won't list it: give it the Mac's name"
      fi
      # The token, read by curl from stdin (never printed): with it the bridge
      # answers, and says where its stream is (from 0.9.0 only with it).
      if [[ -r $tokenfile ]]; then
        code_stream=$(printf 'header = "Authorization: Bearer %s"\nheader = "X-Omarock: 1"\n' "$(tr -d '\n\r"\\' <"$tokenfile")" \
          | curl -s -m 5 -K - -w '\n%{http_code}' "$bridge/v1/status" 2>/dev/null | tail -1)
        if [[ $code_stream == 401 ]]; then
          bad "the bridge refused omarock's token: pair again (./install pair on the Mac, then its code in the settings' Apple Music tab)"
        elif [[ $code_stream == 200 ]]; then
          ok "the bridge accepts omarock's token"
          stream=$(printf 'header = "Authorization: Bearer %s"\nheader = "X-Omarock: 1"\n' "$(tr -d '\n\r"\\' <"$tokenfile")" \
            | curl -s -m 5 -K - "$bridge/v1/health" 2>/dev/null \
            | python3 -I -c 'import json, sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin).get("stream") or "")' 2>/dev/null)
          [[ -n $stream ]] && ok "the bridge gives omarock its stream" || bad "the bridge doesn't say where its stream is"
        fi
      fi
    else
      bad "the bridge doesn't answer at $bridge (is the Mac awake, and can this machine reach it?)"
    fi
  fi
  # From 0.7.0 the bridge's stream keeps a stock libFLAC in step; omarock's
  # patched one (from before) can go.
  pid=$(systemctl --user show -p MainPID --value mpd 2>/dev/null)
  patched=false
  [[ -n $pid && $pid != 0 ]] && grep -q omarock-flac "/proc/$pid/maps" 2>/dev/null && patched=true
  if [[ -n ${h:-} ]] && python3 -I -c 'import json, sys; sys.exit(json.load(sys.stdin).get("minBitrate") is not True)' <<<"$h" 2>/dev/null; then
    if $patched; then
      note "mpd still loads omarock's patched libFLAC, which the bridge's stream no longer needs: ./install apple-music offers to remove it"
    else
      ok "the bridge's stream keeps mpd in step"
    fi
  elif [[ -n ${h:-} ]]; then
    note "the bridge is older than 0.7.0: update it (git pull, then ./install, in the Mac's omarock clone); until then omarock reconnects mpd after each change"
  fi
fi
echo
